# No nested QEventLoop on the UI thread

`waitWithProgress` plus a modal `QProgressDialog` must not call `QEventLoop::exec()`. A second loop on the UI thread re-enters `start`/`cancel`, misses `finished`, and can deadlock. Keep the FFmpeg `QProcess` async; only the wait helper pumps events.

Poll `QCoreApplication::processEvents` until a terminal flag (`finished_` / `isTerminal()`). `setAutoClose(false)` and `setAutoReset(false)` so the dialog cannot close itself and re-enter handlers. Disconnect cancel when the wait ends. `QSignalBlocker` around `close()`.

```cpp
// BAD — nested exec re-enters slots while the caller is still in loadVideoFromFile
QEventLoop loop;
connect(this, &Preparer::preparationFinished, &loop, &QEventLoop::quit);
progress.show();
loop.exec();

// GOOD — same thread, no extra loop; cancel still reaches cancel()
progress.setAutoClose(false);
progress.setAutoReset(false);
const auto cancelConnection =
    connect(&progress, &QProgressDialog::canceled, this, &Preparer::cancel);
progress.show();
while (!finished_) {
  QCoreApplication::processEvents(QEventLoop::AllEvents, 100);
}
disconnect(cancelConnection);
```
